      "side": 1,
      "message": "Every vendor/product variant module has its own VndkVersion that was assigned on image mutation (https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/soong/cc/cc.go;l\u003d3193?q\u003df:cc.go%20vndkversion).\nThis could be different by some reasons (Some modules are using BOARD_VNDK_VERSION but some may use PRODUCT_PRODUCT_VNDK_VERSION, or some may use `current` even BOARD_VNDK_VERSION is not `current`.)\nSo we need to follow the VNDK version in the module instead of using a single version for all modules.\n\nBut I am not sure if we need abi dump checks for `not ctx.useVndk()` case which must be core variants. Moreover, as image variants use the same source tree, they must have the same vndkVersion.",
      "parentUuid": "e699a3b4_ef35e0d2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1082,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 1082,
        "endChar": 18
